{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aether/1520881-aether-societies","id":1520881,"title":"Aether Societies?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aether"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-18T07:57:10-07:00","id":1520881,"title":"Aether Societies?","content":"Does anyone have a list of the Societies and Counter Societies from Aether?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T08:04:32-07:00","id":1520882,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Societies</u></b><br /> The Esoteric Order of the \u00c6ons<br /> Edison's Unwinders<br /> Her Royal Highness's Planetary Defensive Pact<br /> The Society for the Opposition of Monsters<br /> Students of Tesla<br /> The Three Prongs<br /> <u><i>Minor</i></u><br /> Blood of Gog<br /> Chevaliers d'If<br /> Os Viajantes<br /> <br /> <b><u>Counter Societies</u></b><br /> The Caesar Consortium<br /> The Children of Mars<br /> The Immortals<br /> Dr. Jekyll's Explorers of the Unknown<br /> Kinou no Bishi, the Warriors for Yesterday<br /> The Order of Murder","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T08:11:15-07:00","id":1520883,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Most of them I can guess from either the names and bits from the previews, but what are the Three Prongs, Blood of Gog, Chevaliers, Viajantes, and Kinou no Bishi?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T08:20:30-07:00","id":1520885,"title":"","content":"Five excerpts: <br /> <br /> Games centered on the Three Prongs focus on mystical intrigue and introspection. The Prongs seek to understand and transcend their mortal bodies using Aether to reach the ultimate escape from humanity as a Magog. While other societies catalog the abilities and events around the use of Aether, the Prongs foster a spiritual understanding of it, but this doesn\u2019t exempt the Prongs from their share of conspiracies or libel when people misinterpret their teachings.<br /> <br /> Games focused on the Blood of Gog allow characters to delve into the world of the occult and test the limits of their power. Finding a Gog on the edge of losing control and helping them regain their sense of self lends well to themes about the cost of power, identity, overcoming addiction, and just what makes us human.<br /> <br /> Games featuring Chevaliers d\u2019If can range from gritty espionage stories to daring exploits to elaborate plots of political intrigue in the name of justice. As a Chevalier, marginalized characters shine as they perform heroic rescues, daunting escapes, and expert cons, lending well to themes of morality and the definition of justice beneath the shadow of ambiguity coming from a place of vengeance.<br /> <br /> Games involving Os Viajantes focus on exploring strange new dimensions through astral projection and the intersection of the metaphysical and scientific. Travelers in their expeditions into the great unknown find themselves in another realm, planet, or pocket of time facing eldritch horrors, aliens, or dinosaurs. The society chronicles these \u201cLost Worlds,\u201d using astronomy to determine whether they\u2019re visiting the same places but at different times or in different locations. Survival in hostile environments is a strong theme Viajantes games can provide; after all, the trick to traveling isn\u2019t reaching the destination but making it home with all their pieces attached. In mixed group games, Viajantes characters may join or lead an expedition offering their unique knowledge of dimensional travel.<br /> <br /> What we call the Victorian era is an exciting time all over the world, with many places all discovering and modernizing at the same time in different ways. To focus only on England or even only on Europe would miss everything else going on in 1895. Using the Kinou no Bushi lets you look at what\u2019s going on in other parts of the world. The Warriors for Yesterday are an interesting microcosm of nationalism and holding on to the past in a disenfranchised social class that could have moved on into industry and wealth but instead focused on what they lost. If you want to play with time travel and paradoxes, as well just want to pit your players against literal samurai, this society may be perfect for you.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T09:48:49-07:00","id":1520893,"title":"","content":"In a nutshell...<br /> <b>Three Prongs</b> = mystical band Hindu alchemists, seeing Aether as spiritual power<br /> <b>Blood of Gog</b> = African Gog cultivists and their inhumanity<br /> <b>Chevaliers</b> = <a href=\"https://queerasfact.podbean.com/e/the-chevaliere-deon-part-1/\" target=\"_blank\">Chevalier d'Eon</a> supporters<br /> <b>Viajantes </b>= Brazilian-European Indiana Jones in 1890s<br /> <b>Kinou no Bushi</b> = Samurais wanting to recreate Edo Japan ( with temporal powers to do it! )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}